#: ../drivers/uvk5_cn.py:485
msgid ""
"This is an experimental driver for Quansheng UV-K5/UV-K6 radios running expanded Chinese third-party firmware (LOSEHU, LTS, UVE), which store channel names as GB2312 and use the split address EEPROM commands.\n"
"\n"
"It has been verified against one such radio, a LOSEHU131HS build: downloading, uploading and a whole-image read-back were checked there. Other builds in this family may behave differently, and a wrong write can harm your radio. Use at your own risk, and keep the image you download before changing anything: it can be used to restore the radio.\n"
"\n"
"- Writing at or above 0x40000 would overwrite the multi-bootloader that some of these builds install there, so this driver never writes that high and refuses an image that extends into it.\n"
"- The default EEPROM size is derived from the reported firmware version and is only a guess; check the \"EEPROM size\" setting against your radio before uploading.\n"
"- Settings (keys, DTMF, MDC, scan lists, boot logo, satellite data, calibration) are not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../drivers/uvk5.py:694
msgid ""
"This is an experimental driver for the Quansheng UV-K5. It may harm your radio, or worse. Use at your own risk.\n"
"\n"
"Before attempting to do any changes please download the memory image from the radio with chirp and keep it. This can be later used to recover the original settings. \n"
"\n"
"some details are not yet implemented"
msgstr ""
"Quansheng UV-K5 用は実験的なドライバです。\n"
"無線機が正常に動作しなくなる可能性があります。すべて自己責任でご利用ください。\n"
"\n"
"変更を行う前に無線機からダウンロードしたデータを保存しておくようにしてください。\n"
"バックアップがあれば問題が発生してもオリジナルの状態に戻すことができます。\n"
"いくつかの設定に関してはまだ実装されていません。"

